# Configuration & Setup

## MCP Server Configuration

The server supports many CLI options:

- `--headless` - Run without UI
- `--browser-url` - Connect to existing Chrome instance
- `--web-ui` - Enable tool toggles web UI (default: true, port 7332)
- `--tool-config` - Path to tool enable/disable JSON
- `--channel` - Chrome channel (stable, canary, beta, dev)
- `--user-data-dir` - Chrome profile directory
- `--isolated` - Use temporary profile (cleaned up after)

## Tool Management Web UI

- Automatically starts at `http://localhost:7332`
- Manage which tools are enabled/disabled
- Settings persisted to `.chrome-devtools-mcp-tools.json`
- Changes communicated via `tools/list_changed` notification (no restart needed)
